+SRST
+``-checkpoint mode=MODE[,option=value...]``
+    Enable checkpoint creation for workload analysis and simulation.
+    
+    The ``mode`` specifies the checkpointing strategy:
+    
+    - ``simpoint``: Use SimPoint analysis files to create checkpoints at
+      representative simulation points. Requires ``simpoint-dir`` to be specified.
+    
+    - ``uniform``: Create checkpoints at uniform instruction intervals.
+    
+    - ``sync-uniform``: Create synchronized checkpoints across multiple cores.
+    
+    Common options:
+    
+    - ``interval=N``: Create checkpoint every N instructions (required)
+    
+    - ``warmup=N``: Execute N instructions before starting checkpointing
+    
+    - ``output-dir=PATH``: Directory for checkpoint output (default: ./checkpoints)
+    
+    - ``workload=NAME``: Workload name for checkpoint organization
+    
+    SimPoint mode options:
+    
+    - ``simpoint-dir=PATH``: Directory containing ``simpoints.txt`` and
+      ``simpoint_weights.txt`` from SimPoint analysis
+    
+    Multi-core options:
+    
+    - ``sync-interval=N``: Synchronize cores every N instructions
+    
+    Examples:
+    
+    ``-checkpoint mode=simpoint,interval=100000000,simpoint-dir=./simpoints``
+    
+    ``-checkpoint mode=uniform,interval=1000000000,output-dir=./checkpoints``
+ERST
